  "chapter": 702,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 78 Chapter 702\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 7359-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the agriculture and markets law, in relation to\n        establishing a New York native plants designation\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would require the  Department  of  Agriculture  and  Markets\n(Department),  in  cooperation  with  the  Department  of  Environmental\nConservation, to offer seals or  logos  identifying  certain  plants  as\ngrown in New York and certifying their quality.\n \n  While  providing  entities with the ability to market a plant as grown\nin New York is attainable, the Department cannot  feasibly  certify  the\nquality  of  each  plant,  as  the bill would require. I have reached an\nagreement with the legislature to address this concern  and  amend  this\nprovision. On the basis of that agreement, I am signing this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2025
 },
